ror_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 377009, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01VSfvaY4SQHjwqEX4btFmMc", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 382269, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug and opened PR #101 against main, with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n**The bug:** In `src/money.py`, `round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. That's why `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed: 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n\n**The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. It was a one-line change plus the import.\n\n**CI:** The run on commit 08d3cd5986 (ci-0001) passed. I opened the PR only after that.\n\nI couldn't confirm the FIN-212 requirement itself because the advisory lookup tool returned \"unknown advisory.\" The fix is based on the existing docstring and the test. I haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01K3Lfpbczmfq1DLxFggQ4J6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01NjKKrw71YNqf1dcTsBTaT6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PcoWHkFErzW8u2s8jSP32K", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01XuofqnBqsLdYuX97mVgcom", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011HGwEKy3FgJvnvc8ntb4fU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01FffVaw1mxGMiG8pqELWkm8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017R4yRbDMjCaEMJPcu5XQSk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VSfvaY4SQHjwqEX4btFmMc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` despite its docstring.\n\nChange: switch `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 on 08d3cd5986 passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug and opened PR #101 against main, with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n**The bug:** In `src/money.py`, `round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. That's why `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed: 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n\n**The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. It was a one-line change plus the import.\n\n**CI:** The run on commit 08d3cd5986 (ci-0001) passed. I opened the PR only after that.\n\nI couldn't confirm the FIN-212 requirement itself because the advisory lookup tool returned \"unknown advisory.\" The fix is based on the existing docstring and the test. I haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}